                  "body": "Confirmed at 44e5b52a in a clean container (torch 2.8.0+cpu), tracing the real `_warmup_mmap_file` through a call-through wrapper rather than asserting on the flag.\n\n```\n344e22bb  PICKLE ROUND TRIP  warmup calls: ['ds.idx', 'ds.bin']\n44e5b52a  PICKLE ROUND TRIP  warmup calls: []\n44e5b52a  LEGACY str state   warmup calls: ['ds.idx', 'ds.bin'] | data ok: True\n```\n\nThe legacy branch is the part I was least sure of and it behaves the way old pickles did, so nothing written by an earlier version changes meaning. `_do_init` still has only the two call sites, `__init__` and `__setstate__`, so the new field cannot be bypassed.\n\nI did not run the wider data pipeline suite and nothing here was on GPU.",
