      "body": "<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n## Copilot review overview\n\n### 🟢 Approval recommended\n\nThe implementation is backward-compatible and comprehensively tests the reported failure modes.\n\n**Review effort:** Balanced  \n**Findings:** None\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>What changed in this PR</strong></summary>\n\nRestores `MMapIndexedDataset` correctly during unpickling while preserving its warmup behavior.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Serializes both the dataset path and `skip_warmup`.\n- Supports legacy path-only pickle states.\n- Adds round-trip and spawned DataLoader coverage.\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| `indexed_dataset.py` | Preserves initialization settings across pickling. |\r\n| `test_data.py` | Tests warmup settings, dtypes, legacy states, and spawned workers. |\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/new/master?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>",
